# The dialogue of an NPC that did not exist a moment ago.
#
# Station 12 spawns a Rootling Merchant tagged @spawned_helper, and this file is bound to that tag, so the
# NPC arrives able to talk. Without the tag a spawned NPC can only ever have whatever dialogue its role
# already had, which is why "spawn a guard, then talk to the guard" could not be written before.
#
# It also despawns itself rather than the station. Station 12 used to offer "despawn me", which retired the
# station in the middle of a walk and took its renamed nameplate with it.

npc: @spawned_helper
title: Spawned helper
speaker: Helper

== start
I did not exist a moment ago. Station 12 spawned me and tagged me @spawned_helper, and this dialogue is bound
to that tag rather than to my role, so it is mine.
-> What does that prove?
    <<jump why>>
-> Send me away
    <<jump leave>>
-> Nothing, thanks
    <<end>>

== why
That a spawned NPC can be a full participant. Every other Rootling Merchant on this server keeps its own
dialogue; only the one that was spawned with the tag has this one.
-> Send me away
    <<jump leave>>
-> Good
    <<end>>

== leave
Back to nothing, then.
<<despawn>>
